## Proof

**Setup.** As $a$ ranges over $\{0,\dots,2016\}$, $\omega^a$ ranges over all $2017$-th roots of unity (each once). As $b$ ranges over $\{0,\dots,2018\}$, $\zeta^b$ ranges over all $2019$-th roots of unity (each once). Note $2017$ is prime and $2019 = 3\times 673$, so $\gcd(2017,2019)=1$; the only common root of $x^{2017}-1$ and $x^{2019}-1$ is $x=1$.

Setting $\alpha = \omega^a$, $\beta = \zeta^b$, the product becomes
$$P = \prod_{\substack{\alpha^{2017}=1,\;\beta^{2019}=1\\(\alpha,\beta)\neq(1,1)}}(\alpha - \beta).$$

**Split by $\alpha = 1$ vs $\alpha \neq 1$:**
$$P = \underbrace{\prod_{\substack{\beta^{2019}=1\\\beta\neq 1}}(1-\beta)}_{A}\;\cdot\;\underbrace{\prod_{\substack{\alpha^{2017}=1\\\alpha\neq 1}}\;\prod_{\beta^{2019}=1}(\alpha-\beta)}_{B}.$$

**Computing $A$.** Since $\prod_{\beta^{2019}=1}(x-\beta)=x^{2019}-1$, we have
$$A = \prod_{\substack{\beta^{2019}=1\\\beta\neq 1}}(1-\beta) = \lim_{x\to 1}\frac{x^{2019}-1}{x-1} = 2019\cdot 1^{2018} = 2019.$$

**Computing $B$.** For fixed $\alpha$ with $\alpha^{2017}=1$:
$$\prod_{\beta^{2019}=1}(\alpha-\beta) = \alpha^{2019}-1.$$
Since $\alpha^{2017}=1$ and $2019 = 2017 + 2$, we get $\alpha^{2019} = \alpha^{2017}\cdot\alpha^{2} = \alpha^{2}$. Thus
$$B = \prod_{\substack{\alpha^{2017}=1\\\alpha\neq 1}}(\alpha^{2}-1).$$

Because $2017$ is prime, every $\alpha\neq 1$ with $\alpha^{2017}=1$ is a primitive $2017$-th root. Since $\gcd(2,2017)=1$, the map $\alpha\mapsto\alpha^{2}$ is a bijection on the set of primitive $2017$-th roots. Therefore, with $\gamma = \alpha^{2}$:
$$B = \prod_{\substack{\gamma^{2017}=1\\\gamma\neq 1}}(\gamma - 1).$$

Using $\prod_{\gamma^{2017}=1}(x-\gamma)=x^{2017}-1$:
$$\prod_{\substack{\gamma^{2017}=1\\\gamma\neq 1}}(1-\gamma) = \lim_{x\to 1}\frac{x^{2017}-1}{x-1} = 2017.$$
There are $2016$ factors (even number), so
$$B = \prod_{\substack{\gamma^{2017}=1\\\gamma\neq 1}}(\gamma-1) = (-1)^{2016}\prod_{\substack{\gamma^{2017}=1\\\gamma\neq 1}}(1-\gamma) = 1\cdot 2017 = 2017.$$

**Combining.**
$$P = A\cdot B = 2019 \times 2017 = (2018+1)(2018-1) = 2018^{2}-1 = 4\,072\,324 - 1 = 4\,072\,323.$$

$$\boxed{P = 2017 \times 2019 = 4\,072\,323}$$

